ease in the number of Scions, including the PCs? I thought it was to fight the newly-escaped Titans. And yes, I'm asking about 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our society is held together by the thinnest of threads: that exquisitely refined sense of tribal order.<br /> Edith Wharton, The Age of Innocence<br /> <br /> I am a huge fan of both the Trinity Universe and the classic World of Darkness.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12799-spellfire22","name":"Spellfire22","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T16:14:51-07:00","id":1094331,"title":"","content":"We don't know for a fact that there is a sudden increase Scions in the 2e universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T17:42:12-07:00","id":1094361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spellfire22</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094281-how-many-times-have-the-titans-tried-to-escape?p=1094301#post1094301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the case, then what's causing the sudden increase in the number of Scions, including the PCs? I thought it was to fight the newly-escaped Titans. And yes, I'm asking about 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In 1E, the Gods chose to withdraw from mortals, leading to the decline of Scions until the Titan's liberation forced them to start looking for more recruits. But in 2E, the Gods largely chose to stay in contact with mortals, or so we've been lead to believe. So it's very possible that Scions have been appearing all throughout history, without the need for some great crisis to encourage the deities to get busy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T19:51:50-07:00","id":1094759,"title":"","content":"Many Pantheons wouldn't even know how to imprison a Titan. The Sh\u00e9n, for example, prefer to give Titans jobs in the Celestial Bureaucracy in hopes of rehabilitating them. The \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0 and Loa, as usual, would like to take this opportunity to remind you there's no such thing as a Titan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"att