cation that their Titans are worthy of imprisonment! Geb and Nut are dear friends, as are the entire Ogdoad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T22:08:26-07:00","id":1094778,"title":"","content":"And all this is why I VASTLY prefer the 2nd ed setting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T23:46:54-07:00","id":1094792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094281-how-many-times-have-the-titans-tried-to-escape?p=1094777#post1094777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e, there have always been Gods and their Scions, which is why The World is a distinct setting unto itself.<br /> <br /> And I think the Netjer would resent the implication that their Titans are worthy of imprisonment! Geb and Nut are dear friends, as are the entire Ogdoad.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ogdoad are Primordials, according to Neall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T00:03:15-07:00","id":1094793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094281-how-many-times-have-the-titans-tried-to-escape?p=1094792#post1094792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Ogdoad are Primordials, according to Neall.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aren't Primordials and Titans kind of a square-rectangle situation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T01:14:30-07:00","id":1094796,"title":"","content":"I got the sense from all earlier posts that they are going with the whole Primordials &gt; Titans &gt; Gods thing, wherein Primordials are 1st generation (and extremely abstract, distant, or alien) divinities and Gods as we know them would be 3rd generation. It's an approach which I found refreshing since it removes the idea of &quot;greater titans&quot; being these quasi-sentient planes of force to which titans are merely terminal interfaces, and assigns an actual name &amp; personality to underlying cosmic forces of the universe that stand apart from direct interaction. A primordial is a being that existed before there was really sentience or substance in the universe, they're ones who actually started everything. Everyone who came later just started building on the property they cleared/created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T01:19:08-07:00","id":1094800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094281-how-many-times-have-the-titans-tried-to-escape?p=1094793#post1094793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't Primordials and Titans kind of a square-rectangle situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Neall indicated something like that early on, but it appears to have been dropped.<br /> <br /> As it currently stands, metaphysically speaking Titans are deities who are wrapped up in their Purviews, lacking any regard, any connection, to humanity. Primordials are entities of such grand concept they generally can't manifest in the World, appearing only in the Overworld, and even then in world-body form.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T03:49:07-07:00","id":1094826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094281-how-many-times-have-the-titans-tried-to-escape?p=1094800#post1094800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> As it currently stands, metaphysically speaking Titans are deities who are wrapped up in their Purviews, lacking any regard, any connection, to humanity. Primordials are entities of such grand concept they generally can't manifest in the World, appearing only in the Overworld, and even then in world-body form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Meaning that if a Scion decided to build their Legend around their purviews, they could in theory become a Titan upon reaching apotheosis?<br /> <br /> I really like that idea; gives players more incentive to try stories in which they work <i>against</i> the Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"